{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790609494,"nonce":"Y8xmL2YfDgitk7lpSo8RXAbWUaw=","message":"Fix (uncommitted): `call_compiled_function` in crates/ash_interp/src/interpreter/mod.rs\nnow takes the bytecode and func_idx. When an HREF argument points at an interpreter\nregister slot (`ref_targets_register`), the value is written into a native-width scratch\nword on the Rust stack (`write_raw_kind` at the pointee kind from the function type;\ndynamic pointees boxed first), the callee gets the scratch address, and afterwards the\nword is read back (`read_raw_kind`) into the slot, also when the call throws. Signatures\nwith no HREF argument take the old path unchanged. More than eight staged refs refuses\nthe compiled entry, which falls back to the interpreter. The old body is now\n`call_compiled_entry`.\n\nRegression test: crates/ash_cli/tests/ref_args.rs with fixture\ncrates/ash/test/tests/TestRefArgs.hx (+ test_ref_args.hl). A seven-argument driver stays\ninterpreted under `--jit-max-args 6` while callees promote at `--jit-threshold 1`; it\ncovers optional Single/Float/Int/Bool arguments read in the callee and explicit\nhl.Ref\u003cSingle/Float/Int/Bool\u003e written through. Old binary: bad=372741 (cranelift),\n221949 (llvm) of 1,000,000 checks; new: bad=0. Runs with ASH_AIR=0 because of a separate\nAIR bug on the caller side (filed separately).\n\nResults with the fix: Q1 bad=0 in interp, jit, hybrid, and forced cranelift/llvm\npromotion. chimpmonk example: hybrid, hybrid --preset game and hybrid --jit-threshold 1\noutput identical to interp. parity_matrix: 4/4 pass (interp, jit, hybrid_default,\nhybrid_promotion_heavy).\n\nNot caused by this change: osr_retier's\nforced_snapshots_from_ordinary_and_osr_entries_preserve_live_state times out because its\ninterp baseline takes about 122 s against a 120 s guest deadline, the same with the\nbinary from before the change. Its plain=0 hybrid run also logs no `[retier] taken` line\non either binary.","files":null}]}